ty surveys across the tenements and undertook limited detailed geological mapping on the Browns min","platform":"airborne","year":2009,"line_km":3100.0},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":63,"text":"2009 and 2010, Compass commissioned new detailed aeromagnetic, airborne electromagnetic and Falcon gravity surveys across the tenements and undertook limited detailed geological mapping on the Browns mining leases.","platform":"airborne","year":2009},{"method":"gravity","page":63,"text":"new detailed aeromagnetic, airborne electromagnetic and Falcon gravity surveys across the tenements and undertook limited detailed geological mapping on the Browns mining leases.","platform":"airborne","year":2009,"line_spacing_m":25.0},{"method":"magnetics","page":64,"text":"The 2012 Falcon survey incorporated aeromagnetic and radiometric data, and a topographic LiDAR survey flown in 2018 provides high\u2011resolution elevation data for geological and environmental s","platform":"airborne","year":2012},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":64,"text":"The data processing and modelling defined numerous strong conductive and chargeable zones that correlate with AEM anomalies, highlighting t","year":2015,"line_km":27.1},{"method":"radiometrics","page":64,"text":"The 2012 Falcon survey incorporated aeromagnetic and radiometric data, and a topographic LiDAR survey flown in 2018 provides high\u2011resolution elevation data for geological and environmental studies.","platform":"airborne","year":2012},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":270,"text":"ferruginous dolomite horizons; \u2212 Untested airborne electromagnetic (AEM), induced polarisation (IP) and gravity anomalies; \u2212 Structurally controlled uranium mineralization associated with the Whites Formation and Coomalie Dolost","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":270,"text":"weathered contacts and ferruginous dolomite horizons; \u2212 Untested airborne electromagnetic (AEM), induced polarisation (IP) and gravity anomalies; \u2212 Structurally controlled uranium mineralization associated with the Whites Format","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"radiometrics","page":270,"text":"\u2212 Gold-platinum-palladium mineralization associated with breccia zones and radiometric anomalies; and \u2212 Industrial mineral potential related to magnesite and phosphate alteration systems."},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":271,"text":"The airborne electromagnetic datasets and follow-up IP traverses identified numerous conductive and chargeable anomalie","platform":"airborne","year":2012},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":271,"text":"the tenure package has been covered by airborne magnetic, radiometric, electromagnetic and Falcon gravity surveys, together with multiple ground induced polarisation (IP) surveys.","platform":"airborne","year":2010},{"method":"gravity","page":271,"text":"covered by airborne magnetic, radiometric, electromagnetic and Falcon gravity surveys, together with multiple ground induced polarisation (IP) surveys.","platform":"airborne","year":2010},{"method":"radiometrics","page":271,"text":"Since 2010, the tenure package has been covered by airborne magnetic, radiometric, electromagnetic and Falcon gravity surveys, together with multiple ground induced polarisation (IP) surveys.","platform":"airborne","year":2010}],"targets":[{"page":270,"explained":true,"untested":true,"text":"contacts and ferruginous dolomite horizons; \u2212 Untested airborne electromagnetic (AEM), induced polarisation (IP) and gravity anomalies; \u2212 Structurally controlled uranium mineralization associated with the Whites Formation and Coomalie Dolostone; \u2212 Gold-platinu"},{"page":271,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"The airborne electromagnetic datasets and follow-up IP traverses identified numerous conductive and chargeable anomalies across both the northern and southern tenement areas. Several of these anomalies remain either untested or only partially drill tested."},{"page":273,"explai